      <level1>
        <h1>Chapter 3: Plays, Poetry, Annotations &amp; Transcriber Notes</h1>
        <level2>
          <h2>3.1 Drama &amp; Dialogue (BANA §13)</h2>
          <p class="bai-stage"><em>[Setting: A high terrace overlooking the ocean at sunset. Enter ELENA and MARCUS.]</em></p>
          <p class="bai-play"><strong>ELENA:</strong> Have you observed the navigation stars tonight? The horizon is completely clear.</p>
          <p class="bai-play"><strong>MARCUS:</strong> <em>(Consulting the marine astrolabe)</em> The coordinates align precisely with the northern chart.</p>
          <p class="bai-stage"><em>[He marks the parchment chart with a brass compass.]</em></p>
        </level2>
        <level2>
          <h2>3.2 Poetry &amp; Stanza Layout (BANA §13)</h2>
          <p class="bai-verse">The tide retreats across the silver sand,</p>
          <p class="bai-verse">Leaving smooth echoes where the breakers rolled;</p>
          <p class="bai-verse">Night casts its quiet shadow on the land,</p>
          <p class="bai-verse">And turns the ocean foam to gleaming gold.</p>
        </level2>
        <level2>
          <h2>3.3 Transcriber Notes &amp; Footnotes</h2>
